{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-42559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-42559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-2){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -8 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6(-28+40) \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-42559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4d5cff37adf02624d9f99dbf6a6ef0bb0425a3c8b89c128316ba855931c658"} {"question" "q-42559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-42559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-504"] ["math" "-58"] ["math" "124"] ["math" "192"] ["math" "72"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-42559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "72"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-1){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4d5cff37adf02624d9f99dbf6a6ef0bb0425a3c8b89c128316ba855931c658"} {"question" "q-91220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -7\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-4){C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91221" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4d5cff37adf02624d9f99dbf6a6ef0bb0425a3c8b89c128316ba855931c658"} {"question" "q-91221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-91221" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}$ equal to zero.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{32}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -11 & 7 & 9 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 7 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4d5cff37adf02624d9f99dbf6a6ef0bb0425a3c8b89c128316ba855931c658"} {"question" "q-132003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -5 & 8\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-2){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10(25+9) \\\\  & =340.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231b5cb0c02dcedf0b2aa0466bc49057d"} {"question" "q-132146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b4d5cff37adf02624d9f99dbf6a6ef0bb0425a3c8b89c128316ba855931c658"} {"question" "q-132146" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071457/state.json" "file_sha256" "26701678773e6bba6538089b6ced8ac231